   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# AI Flotation Analyser\n",
    "## Complete Feature Analysis + Standard and Advanced Models\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook combines the earlier feature-selection workflow with a broader model comparison.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Main objectives\n",
    "1. Audit and understand the extracted flotation features.\n",
    "2. Separate behavioural features from identifiers and quality-control variables.\n",
    "3. Reduce obvious redundancy.\n",
    "4. Explore behaviour profiles with PCA + K-means.\n",
    "5. Train and compare **standard and advanced models** on the temporary exploratory target.\n",
    "6. Compare Accuracy, Balanced Accuracy, Precision, Recall, Macro F1 and Weighted F1.\n",
    "7. Explain the best-performing models with permutation importance, ablation and SHAP.\n",
    "8. Prepare the workflow for the future **expert flotation-quality target**.\n",
    "9. Include advanced future models such as ordinal regression, EBM, GAM-style models, boosted trees, Gaussian processes, PLS and mixed-effects analysis.\n",
    "10. End with a clear model-selection recommendation for the project.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Important:** The current supervised classification target is generated from the same behavioural feature space by PCA + K-means. It is therefore a **pipeline sanity-check**, not independent evidence that the system predicts good or bad flotation. Final performance modelling must use an independent expert/domain label.\n"
   ]
  },
