    "\n",
    "## 7. Correlation heatmap and redundant raw features\n",
    "\n",
    "Spearman correlation is used because it is suitable for monotonic relationships and does not require normal distributions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Very strong absolute correlations indicate possible redundancy. We do not delete a feature from correlation alone; physical meaning and performance against the final expert target also matter.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d1305b1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
